[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two Tuscan chicken and smashed white bean wraps placed on simple, matte off-white ceramic plates. The primary wrap is centered in the foreground, sliced diagonally to reveal the cross-section of the filling, with the second wrap positioned slightly behind and blurred. Camera angle is a 3/4 overhead view at 40 degrees, ensuring the layers of the wrap are clearly identifiable. Shallow depth of field creates a soft natural bokeh background. Soft, natural side light enters from a window on the left, casting gentle, natural shadows and highlighting the texture of the whole-wheat tortillas. The surface is a worn, rustic aged oak table with visible wood grain. Props include a small wooden spoon resting casually beside the plate and a few scattered pieces of sun-dried tomato and a small cluster of fresh baby spinach leaves on the table surface. The filling clearly shows the creamy, pale texture of the smashed cannellini beans binding the chunks of rotisserie chicken, vivid red pieces of chopped sun-dried tomatoes, and light green chopped artichoke hearts, all nestled over a bed of vibrant, fresh baby spinach. The tortillas have a light brown, whole-wheat texture. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene reflects a lived-in, warm home kitchen. Includes slight natural imperfections like a tiny stray spinach leaf and a small, realistic smudge of bean filling on the plate rim. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature, cozy and inviting. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional cookbook photography."
  }
]
